# Default OpenAI API Configuration
# Copy this file to .env and set your actual values

# LLM Provider Configuration
# Supported providers: openai, anthropic, openrouter, ollama
LLM_PROVIDER=openai

# OpenAI Configuration (when LLM_PROVIDER=openai)
OPENAI_API_KEY=
OPENAI_MODEL_NAME=gpt-4.1-2025-04-14

# Anthropic Configuration (when LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic)
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_MODEL_NAME=claude-sonnet-4-20250514

# OpenRouter Configuration (when LLM_PROVIDER=openrouter)
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_MODEL_NAME=google/gemini-2.0-flash-001
OPENROUTER_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1

# Ollama Configuration (when LLM_PROVIDER=ollama)
# Vision-capable models: qwen2.5vl:7b (recommended), gemma3:4b, llama3.2-vision, llava
OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434
OLLAMA_MODEL_NAME=qwen2.5vl:7b

# Ollama-specific prompt template (optimized for visual pattern recognition)
OLLAMA_PROMPT_TEMPLATE="Analyze this resonant angle plot. Y-axis: resonant angle (-π to +π), X-axis: time (0-100000 years).

Look for the MOST OBVIOUS pattern:

1. CLEAR DIAGONAL FLOW (NON-RESONANT):
   - Obvious slanted stripes flowing from corner to corner
   - Data moves continuously across the full plot height
   
2. APOCENTRIC LIBRATION (RESONANT):
   - Data clustered at TOP and BOTTOM edges only
   - EMPTY space in the middle horizontal band
   
3. REGULAR LIBRATION (RESONANT):
   - Data oscillates within a limited range (not reaching plot edges)
   - Horizontal oscillating patterns
   
4. TRANSIENT: Behavior clearly changes over time

Choose the classification that matches the MOST OBVIOUS visual pattern.
When in doubt between apocentric libration and circulation, favor apocentric if there's any empty middle space.

IMPORTANT: Respond with ONLY a JSON object:
{\"status\": \"resonant\", \"subtype\": \"describe the dominant pattern\"}"

# Optional: Custom prompt template for all providers

# General LLM prompt (Claude 4)
# PROMPT_TEMPLATE="Classify the astronomical plot showing resonance argument evolution over time. The plot displays points with y-axis from 0 to 2π representing the resonance argument, and x-axis representing time.\n\nCLASSIFICATION GUIDELINES:\n\n1. RESONANT - Bounded oscillations (libration)\n- Clear libration: Simple sinusoidal oscillations around a fixed center\n- Apocentric libration: Oscillations split between top/bottom of plot due to 2π wrapping. KEY: empty horizontal band in middle where no points exist\n- High amplitude: Large oscillations, possibly overlapping\n- Long period: Very slow oscillations (1-2 periods visible)\n- Noisy: Libration with short-period perturbations creating thick/fuzzy appearance\n- Double: Superposition of high and low frequency oscillations\n\n2. NON-RESONANT - Unbounded motion (circulation)\n- Regular circulation: Parallel diagonal lines at any angle\n- Sparse: Only 3-4 diagonal lines across plot\n- Chaotic: Random scatter of points without structure\n- Mixed: Combination of chaotic regions and circulation lines\n\n3. TRANSIENT - Alternating behaviors\n- Must have BOTH substantial libration (>10% of timespan) AND clear circulation periods\n- Choose subtype based on the dominant pattern or transition sequence\n\n4. CONTROVERSIAL - Use when:\n- Confidence below 70-80%\n- Pattern doesn't clearly fit other categories\n- Provide descriptive explanation of ambiguity\n\nKEY RULES:\n- If libration appears for less than 10% of timespan, classify as non-resonant\n- For apocentric patterns, the empty horizontal band is the key identifier\n- Look past noise to identify underlying patterns\n- Transient requires BOTH behaviors for significant durations\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT:\nReturn a JSON object with:\n- status: one of [\"resonant\", \"non-resonant\", \"transient\", \"controversial\"]\n- subtype: specific pattern from the predefined options above\n\nExample: {\"status\": \"resonant\", \"subtype\": \"noisy libration\"}"

# General LLM prompt (gpt-o3)
# PROMPT_TEMPLATE="You are an astronomer who has inspected thousands of resonant‑angle plots.\n\nInput: one grayscale scatter plot of the resonant argument (y‑axis 0→2π) versus time (x‑axis).\n\nGoal: return a JSON object that fits the LibrationAnalysisResult model shown below, using only the keys \"status\" and \"subtype\".\n\nHigh‑level status classes\n1. resonant        – argument librates for the entire plot.\n2. non-resonant    – argument circulates for the entire plot.\n3. transient       – plot contains both substantial libration and substantial circulation segments (each ≥20 % of width).\n4. controversial   – use only if you cannot reach 80 % confidence in any other class.\n\nVisual cues\n• Librations: continuous bounded oscillation. Variants include\n  clean sinusoid, apocentric (two separated bands with an empty stripe),\n  high‑amplitude, very slow (≤1 visible period), noisy, or double‑frequency.\n• Circulations: straight quasi‑parallel lines of any slope, or a uniform pepper‑noise cloud (fully chaotic).\n  Brief libration patches occupying <10 % of the width do not change the label.\n• Transient: clear blocks of libration and circulation of comparable visual weight.\n• Controversial: ambiguous or conflicting features.\n\nDecision procedure\n1. Inspect the entire width (ignore border artefacts).\n2. Decide which class dominates ≥80 % of the time span.\n3. If no class reaches that confidence, choose controversial.\n4. Pick the most specific subtype phrase that best describes the pattern.\n\nOutput format – exactly this JSON schema, nothing else:\n{\n  \"status\": \"<resonant | non-resonant | transient | controversial>\",\n  \"subtype\": \"<lower‑case descriptive phrase>\"\n}\n\nBegin."

# Ollama small models
PROMPT_TEMPLATE="Analyze the astronomical resonance plot in the image.\n\nThe plot shows:\n- Y-axis: resonance argument (0 to 2π)\n- X-axis: time evolution\n- Black dots: data points\n\nClassification task:\n1. Identify the primary pattern\n2. Select the specific subtype\n3. Return JSON classification\n\nPATTERN DEFINITIONS:\n\nRESONANT (bounded oscillations):\n- clear libration: clean sinusoidal waves\n- noisy libration: waves with fuzzy/thick appearance\n- apocentric libration: oscillations split top/bottom, EMPTY BAND in middle\n- high amplitude libration: large waves, may overlap\n- long period libration: 1-2 slow oscillations visible\n- double libration: mixed frequencies\n\nNON-RESONANT (unbounded motion):\n- circulation: diagonal parallel lines\n- sparse circulation: only 3-4 lines\n- chaotic circulation: scattered points\n- mixed circulation: lines + chaos\n\nTRANSIENT: Both libration AND circulation present (each >10% of plot)\n\nCONTROVERSIAL: Pattern unclear or confidence <80%\n\nExample outputs:\n{\"status\": \"resonant\", \"subtype\": \"noisy libration\"}\n{\"status\": \"non-resonant\", \"subtype\": \"circulation\"}\n{\"status\": \"transient\", \"subtype\": \"alternating libration and circulation\"}\n\nAnalyze the image and respond with the JSON classification."

# PROMPT_TEMPLATE="Your custom prompt template here..."
